      "content": "i get the caution, but if we lead with the nausea rates in the main copy, it's going to kill the momentum of the whole campaign. the executives want a winner, not a disclaimer.\n\nis there any way we can interpret the data so the comfort side still looks dominant? like, if we focus on the *speed* of the relief, can we argue that actually improves the overall patient experience enough to justify the 'comfort' branding, even with the nausea being a minor factor? i need a way to make this work without being totally blatant about it.",
